HashMap is a collection in Java that stores data in Key-Value pairs.

HashMap<Integer, String> map = new HashMap<>();

map.put(1, "Vivek");
map.put(2, "Rahul");
map.put(3, "Amit");

System.out.println(map);

o/p---{1=Vivek, 2=Rahul, 3=Amit}

Problem: HashMap is not thread-safe.

If multiple threads modify the same HashMap without synchronization, the result may be unpredictable.

